63-1042-41fb-859d-61e1ab0f8c5f/c2fbeab0-b840-11ec-a05a-a710251ca16c/file-1l1sah9lo.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1sah9ln/7acb6a63-1042-41fb-859d-61e1ab0f8c5f/c2fbeab0-b840-11ec-a05a-a710251ca16c/file-1l1sah9lo.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1sah9ln/7acb6a63-1042-41fb-859d-61e1ab0f8c5f/c2fbeab0-b840-11ec-a05a-a710251ca16c/file-1l1sah9lo.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1sah9ln/7acb6a63-1042-41fb-859d-61e1ab0f8c5f/c2fbeab0-b840-11ec-a05a-a710251ca16c/file-1l1sah9lo.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1sah9ln/7acb6a63-1042-41fb-859d-61e1ab0f8c5f/c2fbeab0-b840-11ec-a05a-a710251ca16c/file-1l1sah9lo.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"P > Q > R > S"},{"identifier":"B","content":"S > P > R > Q"},{"identifier":"C","content":"P > R > Q > S"},{"identifier":"D","content":"R > P > S > Q"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p> The bulky groups cause steric hindrance in the formation of transition state. Therefore, higher homologues (Q) are less reactive than lower homologues (P). In compound (S), the transition state is highly stabilized by Ph-(C=O)- group, so it has highest rate of reaction towards S<sub>N</sub>2. </p>\n<p>The relative reactivities towards S<sub>N</sub>2 reaction S > P > R > Q.</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"haloalkanes","type":"mcq","year":2013,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2013-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l1ozno5k","chapter":"alcohols-phenols-and-ethers","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2013-paper-1-offline","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 