vanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"pin-the-reaction-p--q-to-r--s-the-time-taken-for-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-jbkefw7ff0rb0qw4","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p>In the reaction, P + Q <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> R + S, the time taken for 75% reaction of P is twice the time taken for 50% reaction of P. The concentration of Q varies with reaction time as shown in the figure. The overall order of the reaction is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Chemical Kinetics and Nuclear Chemistry Question 18 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l1sa0mpc/12f73a84-4557-462c-9b85-0669890299db/f4599f00-b83e-11ec-806c-03799111e271/file-1l1sa0mpd.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"2"},{"identifier":"B","content":"3"},{"identifier":"C","content":"0"},{"identifier":"D","content":"1"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>This is a first-order reaction because t<sub>75%</sub> = 2 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> t<sub>50%</sub>. The graph shows that the order with respect to Q is 0, so we can write the rate expression as</p>\n<p>Rate = k[P]<sup>1</sup>[Q]<sup>0</sup></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"different-methods-to-determine-order-of-reaction","type":"mcq","year":2013,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2013-paper-1-offline","active":true}],"ids":["1l1ozkkdc","1l1ozno5k","1l1ozsf9q","1l1ozvlxr"],"title":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline | JEE Advanced Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app